  "summary": "Unbounded allocation from peer-declared frame length in github.com/gobwas/ws",
  "details": "ws.ReadFrame, ws.MustReadFrame, and the wsutil message readers allocate a buffer of the payload length declared in the frame header before reading any payload bytes. A remote unauthenticated peer can send a frame header declaring a large payload length and cause an out-of-memory crash.",
  "affected": [
